& [Purpose]
  + compose published supplied-value assembly semantic find and exact source excerpt kernels into one bounded replayable inspection transaction

& [SJSProcessing]
  + delineation selects only outer orchestration cross-receipt validation and one outer digest
  + semantic refinement defines success as a complete assembly one exact find page and one positionally corresponding excerpt for every returned hit
  + constraint reapplication preserves every nested kernel bound fault and non-authority while adding stricter composition limits
  + pruning removes host loading caching context expansion ranking transport persistence and runtime concerns
  + seven-fold exhaustion finds no smaller seam that closes caller coordination while retaining exact evidence
  + data-driven design makes supplied project find request nested receipts ordered correspondence and outer receipt the complete data plane

& [Requirements]
  + [CRSI-001] replay the exact four-file published source snapshot at57333 bytes and preserve the protected live C state
  + [CRSI-002] implement one separate safe-Rust effect-free cantor_sop_inspect crate
  + [CRSI-003] define capability kernel.sop.semantic-inspect and request profile cantor-sop-semantic-inspection-request/0.1
  + [CRSI-004] accept exactly one SuppliedProject one FindRequest one fixed page_hits_with_exact_source projection and one request digest
  + [CRSI-005] strictly parse one request value with unknown duplicate trailing malformed and excess-byte refusal
  + [CRSI-006] validate the outer request digest before assembly query or excerpt work
  + [CRSI-007] call the published project assembler without changing its semantics
  + [CRSI-008] require a complete diagnostic-free assembly before query
  + [CRSI-009] call the published semantic finder without changing ambiguity filters cursor or pagination semantics
  + [CRSI-010] limit a composed find page to at most64 hits even when the nested finder permits more
  + [CRSI-011] call the published source excerpt kernel once for each returned hit in exact page order
  + [CRSI-012] require each excerpt record identity to equal its corresponding find-hit unit identity
  + [CRSI-013] require every nested assembly result generation query and request binding to agree
  + [CRSI-014] return compact assembly coordinates the exact FindResult ordered exact SourceExcerptResults non-authority and one outer result digest
  + [CRSI-015] preserve empty result pages and paginated continuation truth exactly
  + [CRSI-016] return no successful partial result when any nested operation refuses
  + [CRSI-017] bound request result excerpt count and aggregate returned excerpt bytes before unbounded work or allocation
  + [CRSI-018] provide deterministic replay validation that reproduces the exact outer result or refuses
  + [CRSI-019] promote only kernel.sop.semantic-inspect through the instance contract while holding whole cantor_scribe
  + [CRSI-020] expose no ambient path filesystem database cache transport process clock random environment provider model operator update remote or effect input
  + [CRSI-021] cover constructive ambiguity Unicode empty pagination and deterministic replay behavior in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CRSI-022] cover reorder omission duplication substitution cross-generation digest bounds machine-form and nested-fault attacks
  + [CRSI-023] pass exact workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host source and independent evidence gates
  + [CRSI-024] attribute publish and immediately bookend only after completion signature direct remote equality and zero-effect replay

& [AcceptanceGates]
  + [CRSI-A01] one valid request yields one exact source-bearing find page with deterministic outer receipt
  + [CRSI-A02] every nested and cross-receipt tamper refuses independently
  + [CRSI-A03] static absence proves caller-owned values are the only data plane
  + [CRSI-A04] focused and complete workspace evidence agree with zero failures and governed ignores only
  + [CRSI-A05] publication records exact implementation and immediate bookend commits without merge or runtime authority

& [Excluded]
  + host source loading SQLite persistence cache durable index context windows ranking neighborhood completion evaluation references authoring LSP MCP resident process provider model inference installation update remote machine product effect and merge

& [Status]
  + formed_for_exact_bounded_implementation_only
